From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:12:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/34] coherent: a held batch copies in what the CPU wrote
 before its signal (E1 copy in)

The last open E1 path: a command buffer committed to wait for a shared event
draws over a trapping surface the guest writes before it sets the event. The
encoder took the image's standing as it was encoded (Coherent::taking found no
CPU write then), so it recorded no copy in, and the draw ran over the image
without the write Metal's draw sees.

The copy in is now decided as the held batch goes:

- shadow::LateCopies (in ShadowCarry): encode_wait_for_event on a shared event
  marks the command buffer; from then on an encoder that takes a trapping
  surface's standing (shadow_lazy's take answered Some) notes the surface,
  once. A surface an earlier encoder of the same command buffer left writes
  ahead in is not noted (Lazy::left_open_by): the copy in would replace them
  with the pages' bytes. A texture copied in at its use needs nothing: that
  copy reads the pages as the GPU runs it. An MTLEvent wait adds nothing.
- submit_batch, after place(): record_late_copies_in takes the noted surfaces
  that the batch's parts use, and for each asks Coherent::taking_late, which
  answers the guest's rectangle (and holds the open pages, as taking does), or
  nothing where the CPU wrote nothing. The copies go in one command buffer at
  the start of the batch's first part, their uses joined to its summary, so
  the barrier the tracker plans before the part orders them after earlier
  writers, then a barrier before the part's own work.
- taking_late runs under the scheduler's lock and waits for no record: a write
  of another command buffer still running over the rectangle is counted
  (overwrite_risk, CoherentFallbackCounts::late_copies_in_busy) where taking
  would wait for a bounded time. The command buffer's own records run after
  the copy and are not counted as busy.
- Counted: CoherentFallbackCounts::late_copies_in, late_copies_in_busy.

Cost where nothing changed: nothing unless a command buffer waits for a
shared event and then takes a trapping surface's standing; then one surface
lock per noted surface when its batch goes, and no command buffer.

Lane surface_coherent_a_cpu_write_before_a_signal_reaches_a_waiting_command is
no longer ignored, and it also checks that late_copies_in moved by one.

Lanes (filters "surface" and "event", ANV, one run): 154 passed, 1 failed,
6 ignored before; 155 passed, 1 failed, 5 ignored after. The failure is
ycbcr_textures::textures_over_any_surface_read_what_metal_reads, as before.
Runtime unit tests: 1149 passed, 2 failed. exit_guard fails as before (the
same two submit.rs Stamps lines). driver_defects'
a_set_past_the_drivers_support_is_among_its_variants_kinds stops on a missing
llvm-as in the build container, before anything this commit touches.

